  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The angular speed of truck wheel is increased from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>900</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rpm</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2460</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rpm</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>26</mn></math> seconds. The number of revolutions by the truck engine during this time is ______.</p><p>(Assuming the acceleration to be uniform).</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "728",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>Let number of revolutions be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>900</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2460</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>26</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>728</mn></math></p>"
  }
}